  "term": "sleeping sickness",
  "definition": "Sleeping sickness is a parasitic illness spread by flies in parts of Sub-Saharan Africa that can damage the nervous system. In addition to early physical symptoms, it can cause confusion, disturbed sleep-wake patterns, and progressive mental decline, and may advance to coma and death if untreated.",
